A||||6||Pheagey||Horn on a '88 coupe||||1||
Z||000000||Pheagey||10-07-2001||09:39 AM||||Where exactly is the horn located? I've looked and looked but am unable to located it exactly. Also, whats the most probable reason for the honr not working (besides the fuse).<BR>Thanx:smile:<P>------------------<BR>Pheagey Grean<BR>"There my hero's, every one of them..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||10-07-2001||09:44 AM||||There's a relay under the right side of the dash. You should hear it clicking when you press the horn button. <BR>The horn is under the left front fender, in front of the wheelwell liner. The connection where the wire clips on to the horn might have crud on it. That's what was wrong with mine.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||10-07-2001||10:45 AM||||If the 88 is like all others years, there is a horn under both fenders, a high and a low tone.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000003||DKOV||10-07-2001||11:24 AM||||My horn quit working because of the connector spring rod thingy under the horn button on the steering wheel...<P>First, the horn would beep every time I went around a corner, then it quit working all together!  Turns out, there is a spring that is supposed to keep a small metal rod from grounding (and completing the circuit) unless you press it down with the horn button.<P>On mine, that spring was shot.  So it was resting on or very near the "ground" and it would touch every so often and sound.<P>Now, it doesn't sound at all...  I took the spring out.  You might want to check to see if your spring and rod are in place correctly too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-07-2001||02:11 PM||||Location.... in the corners under the facia, outside the frame, one in front of each wheel well. you'll need to slighty jack the car for easier access.<P>there are more notes in my cave....<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rodmcneill||10-07-2001||09:04 PM||||88 Fiero's only came with one horn,I guess they had to save some money after the suspension upgrade. I am going to install Italian dual horns this winter, one horn sounds really cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rick 88||10-08-2001||01:31 AM||||Rod is correct. The 88's got one cheap plastic horn. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I backdated mine to 87 dual horns. Now it sounds like a Fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rick 88<BR>yellow GT 5-speed (with good horns)||||reg||1
